'''Kami''' is a [[Nupoid language]] spoken in [[Niger State]], [[Nigeria]]. Kami is spoken only in Ebo town, located to the south of [[Lapai]]. There are at most 500 speakers. Kami is closely related to Gupa and Dibo.

There is also a fishing group known as '''Kede''' ('''Kyadya, Kiadia, Kyedye''') who speak the same language.<ref name="Blench2013">Blench, Roger. 2013. ''[http://www.rogerblench.info/Language/Niger-Congo/VN/Nupoid/Nupoid%20Overview%202013.pdf The Nupoid languages of west-central Nigeria: overview and comparative word list]''.</ref>

